We are given the vertices of a convex pentagon: $(-1,-1), (-3,4), (1,7), (6,5)$ and $(3,-1)$. We want to find the area of the pentagon. 
We can use the Shoelace Theorem to compute the area. The Shoelace Theorem states that if the vertices of a polygon are $(x_1, y_1), (x_2, y_2), \dots, (x_n, y_n)$ in order, then the area of the polygon is 
